questions.questionText:
If the matrix $$A = \left[ {\matrix{
1 & 0 & 0 \cr
0 & 2 & 0 \cr
3 & 0 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right]$$ satisfies the equation

$${A^{20}} + \alpha {A^{19}} + \beta A = \left[ {\matrix{
1 & 0 & 0 \cr
0 & 4 & 0 \cr
0 & 0 & 1 \cr

} } \right]$$ for some real numbers $$\alpha$$ and $$\beta$$, then $$\beta$$ $$-$$ $$\alpha$$ is equal to ___________.

